00:26:03.583 --> 00:26:04.583
Greetings

00:26:04.583 --> 00:26:05.791
I'm their second cousin 

00:26:06.874 --> 00:26:08.958
This little guy is Gundy Van Gundy

00:26:09.249 --> 00:26:13.458
He’s severely gundied, so don’t say nothing about
“load management” in front of that one

00:26:13.458 --> 00:26:16.499
Ah! That'll ruin the game and you know it!

00:26:16.499 --> 00:26:18.708
All right. Ethan, can you show the knights to their chambers? 

00:26:19.291 --> 00:26:21.458
Our training begins bright and early tomorrow

00:26:27.833 --> 00:26:30.416
If you can’t make your free throws, they’re gonna hack you all day

00:26:33.583 --> 00:26:38.458
I don’t know, I just sorta feel like…I don’t need analytics to tell me LeBron is good

00:26:38.458 --> 00:26:40.833
You know? I know that. I can see that

00:26:41.708 --> 00:26:45.333
Ugh, I’m just not sure this will be enough, Brother Jeff

00:26:45.333 --> 00:26:50.041
The Lords of Detroit will have me head if we don’t make a run in the playoffs this year

00:26:50.041 --> 00:26:53.291
You know, there is another option. I mean, you are the Master of Trades, right?

00:26:53.583 --> 00:26:54.083
Aye

00:26:54.083 --> 00:26:56.499
Well, I hear whispers of a wealthy lord 

00:26:56.499 --> 00:26:59.124
who’s looking to part ways with his most decorated knight

00:26:59.583 --> 00:27:02.416
If I send a raven now, they can be here on the morrow

00:27:02.541 --> 00:27:04.249
Ugh...I just...

00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:07.833
Ah, screw it. Send the raven

00:27:07.833 --> 00:27:12.208
I think you’re gonna like him, Brother Stan. He’s even balder and louder than I

00:27:13.916 --> 00:27:21.416
Developing! Developing! Developing players! Let’s make a trade, baby! Woooo! 

00:27:22.833 --> 00:27:24.291
Ser Blake Griffin

00:27:24.499 --> 00:27:26.333
But he’s the face of your franchise

00:27:26.541 --> 00:27:27.999
And soon he can be the face of yours

00:27:27.999 --> 00:27:34.916
All right, but…who would you want for him? Tobias is a good developing player

00:27:35.249 --> 00:27:36.541
Yes, him

00:27:37.083 --> 00:27:38.624
All right! You’ve got yourself a dea–

00:27:38.624 --> 00:27:42.583
Also Avery Bradley, Boban the Giant and a first-round pick

00:27:42.791 --> 00:27:47.999
I mean...that’s quite a lot. What kind of contract do you got him under?

00:27:47.999 --> 00:27:50.541
Five years. 171 Million

00:27:51.208 --> 00:27:53.749
Seven hells, that’s a lot of gold

00:27:53.749 --> 00:27:54.666
I mean,

00:27:54.666 --> 00:27:57.041
Ser Griffin’s a marvelous talent and all

00:27:57.041 --> 00:27:59.208
Do you know he once dunked over a horse?

00:27:59.541 --> 00:28:00.124
Clydesdale

00:28:00.124 --> 00:28:07.708
Ah, wow, that’s...that’s really athletic. I just...171 million gold...it’s a lot...

00:28:07.708 --> 00:28:11.124
Oh, and did you know, he’s…funny? 

00:28:11.124 --> 00:28:12.916
Oh? Is...is he now...

00:28:13.041 --> 00:28:15.333
Blake, tell us one of your jokes

00:28:15.749 --> 00:28:18.416
Um...sure...yeah

00:28:20.166 --> 00:28:23.874
Uh, so…cheers. Thanks for coming out everyone…um... 

00:28:23.874 --> 00:28:28.499
So my squire year, some of the older blokes take me to a whorehouse—

00:28:28.666 --> 00:28:30.749
Not that one. Not that one

00:28:31.624 --> 00:28:38.291
Right...um...so a ref walks into a bar...and then a table...and then some chairs…

00:28:42.624 --> 00:28:44.791
[laughs]

00:28:44.833 --> 00:28:46.749
Because he’s…because the ref is blind! 

00:28:46.749 --> 00:28:47.791
[laughs]

00:28:47.791 --> 00:28:49.291
That’s great, laddie

00:28:49.916 --> 00:28:50.916
It’s a deal! 

00:28:58.166 --> 00:29:03.749
Fare thee well, House Pistons! And remember, stay away from those analytics folks!

00:29:04.833 --> 00:29:11.208
[chanting]
Alonzo

00:29:11.833 --> 00:29:13.874
[chanting]
Mourning

00:29:16.833 --> 00:29:17.833
What they doing?

00:29:17.833 --> 00:29:22.374
That there is the ceremonial exodus of the Van Gundys. Watch

00:29:22.374 --> 00:29:29.458
[chanting]
Back cut, down screen, ice, ice

00:29:29.499 --> 00:29:34.708
Go forth to victory! And please give our tidings to the maiden Rihanna!

00:29:34.708 --> 00:29:36.833
Bey! Ah, Bey

00:29:36.833 --> 00:29:38.374
I...don’t think she’s a maiden

00:29:38.374 --> 00:29:39.958
[laughs] This lad!

00:29:39.958 --> 00:29:45.083
I've got a feeling we're going to have a long, bright future together, Blake

00:29:53.458 --> 00:29:55.000
[crow cawing]

00:29:55.458 --> 00:29:59.042
Ser Kristaps, are you excited about your new Lord Commander Fizdale?

00:29:59.375 --> 00:30:03.167
Looks like House Knicks won’t be getting rooked any time soon. Huh?

00:30:03.500 --> 00:30:04.167
[crow cawing]

00:30:04.167 --> 00:30:06.125
Fizdale hates European big men!

00:30:06.375 --> 00:30:07.792
Don’t listen to it

00:30:08.083 --> 00:30:10.125
Crows are all liars

00:30:10.125 --> 00:30:10.792
[crow cawing]

00:30:10.792 --> 00:30:12.667
Joakim Noah has a shit contract

00:30:12.875 --> 00:30:14.542
Well, OK, not all crows

00:30:15.167 --> 00:30:17.292
I know a story about a bird

00:30:17.625 --> 00:30:21.542
His name was Larry, and his hair was fair just like yours

00:30:21.542 --> 00:30:24.625
But he had a third eye that could see into the future

00:30:24.875 --> 00:30:26.000
Also a bad back

00:30:26.458 --> 00:30:27.833
I hate your stories

00:30:28.042 --> 00:30:31.583
I know a story about a child who hated stories

00:30:31.750 --> 00:30:35.417
I also know a story about a Chris Childs who punched Kobes

00:30:35.750 --> 00:30:38.708
I could tell you about Ser Ewing the Sweaty

00:30:39.125 --> 00:30:40.958
Those were always your favorite

00:30:40.958 --> 00:30:42.375
Those weren’t my favorites

00:30:42.375 --> 00:30:46.750
I could tell you the tale of Starbury shaggin’ in his wagon with the marketing apprentice

00:30:46.750 --> 00:30:50.667
Is this the sort of salacious and flirtatious story you like?

00:30:50.833 --> 00:30:51.958
Uh...no?

00:30:52.208 --> 00:30:54.542
Maybe you’d like a scary story

00:30:54.542 --> 00:30:58.125
[scoffs] Think you can scare me, Walt...Clyde...whatever your name is?

00:30:58.542 --> 00:31:03.417
There is nothing more frightening than being the second option to Carmelo in the triangle

00:31:04.792 --> 00:31:07.417
Oh, my sweet Latvian child

00:31:07.417 --> 00:31:10.375
What do you know about fear?

00:31:10.792 --> 00:31:16.417
Fear is for the elders who’ve suffered through the entire reign of James Dolan

00:31:16.417 --> 00:31:24.000
Fanlings are born and live and die, all without seeing a playoff win or a decent draft pick

00:31:24.333 --> 00:31:26.542
It was in this darkness

00:31:26.542 --> 00:31:32.750
that Isiah Thomas gave a 5-year contract to Jerome “Big Snacks” James

00:31:32.792 --> 00:31:33.458
Who?

00:31:33.917 --> 00:31:34.917
Exactly

00:31:35.167 --> 00:31:39.167
That is the time for fear, my lanky lord

00:31:39.333 --> 00:31:43.083
Watching Stephon Marbury, Steve Francis and Jamal Crawford

00:31:43.083 --> 00:31:47.375
three shoot-first guards—try to coexist in the same backcourt

00:31:47.792 --> 00:31:50.042
Draft picks busting in their cribs

00:31:50.458 --> 00:31:53.625
Bloated contracts for bloated players

00:31:53.958 --> 00:31:56.375
Women smothered their babies 

00:31:56.375 --> 00:32:00.458
rather than see them watch Eddy Curry get paid 60 million gold

00:32:00.458 --> 00:32:02.500
to eat freakin’ lemon cakes on the bench

00:32:03.500 --> 00:32:05.708
And don’t get me started with Bargnani!

00:32:06.542 --> 00:32:08.958
Fear is for Lord Dolan playing lute,

00:32:08.958 --> 00:32:13.583
and having to tell him he’s razzlin’ and dazzlin’ when inside you’re crying and dying

00:32:13.583 --> 00:32:16.417
but you keep lying and complying because it’s terrifying and—

00:32:16.417 --> 00:32:17.750
[knocking]

00:32:18.125 --> 00:32:19.125
[lute strumming]

00:32:19.125 --> 00:32:20.125
Oh...

00:32:20.458 --> 00:32:24.250
Did I just hear...Lord...ah...Dolan roll–roll in?

00:32:24.250 --> 00:32:27.500
Hello, yes, it is I, Lord Dolan

00:32:27.958 --> 00:32:31.750
Just wanted to stop and sing Kristaps here a little cheer-up song

00:32:32.208 --> 00:32:34.167
Oh, how delightful and exciteful

00:32:34.167 --> 00:32:35.292
[clears throat]

00:32:35.667 --> 00:32:36.375
Here we go

00:32:36.500 --> 00:32:40.458
[lute playing]

00:32:40.875 --> 00:32:42.792
[singing]
Better find a sept

00:32:44.625 --> 00:32:47.333
[singing]
A good place to cry

00:32:49.292 --> 00:32:56.333
[singing]
‘Cause we’re not going to tank or play Frank Ntilikina ‘cause Mudiay’s our guy

00:32:56.958 --> 00:32:58.625
[singing]
Better find a sept

00:33:00.542 --> 00:33:04.542
[singing]
A good place to pray for all your sins

00:33:05.333 --> 00:33:09.167
[singing]
Will I overpay Trey Burke?

00:33:09.167 --> 00:33:12.667
[singing]
Or let him walk away like Jeremy Lin (that jerk!)

00:33:14.083 --> 00:33:16.708
[singing]
And Oakley is still not welcome back

00:33:16.708 --> 00:33:18.583
[singing]
Maybe I’ll re-sign Jarrett Jack

00:33:18.583 --> 00:33:20.500
[singing]
Hell, I’ll pay the luxury tax

00:33:20.500 --> 00:33:25.417
[singing]
to give Tyreke Evans a max five-year contract

00:33:25.417 --> 00:33:26.417
[singing]
Ooo!

00:33:26.417 --> 00:33:29.708
[singing]
I should bring Isiah Thomas back,

00:33:29.708 --> 00:33:34.208
[singing]
and the small one, too, for a longer deal

00:33:34.208 --> 00:33:38.208
[singing]
I think Elfrid Payton is the next Bradley Beal

00:33:38.208 --> 00:33:40.667
All right, Krislaps Porzmingis

00:33:40.667 --> 00:33:42.583
Time for you to hurry up and heal

00:33:42.583 --> 00:33:45.833
A little birdie told me Fizdale hates his European big men

00:33:45.833 --> 00:33:46.833
[laughs]

00:33:46.833 --> 00:33:48.167
Talk to you later, buddy

00:33:48.167 --> 00:33:49.583
See you in Lithuania

00:33:49.583 --> 00:33:51.250
Where's Oakley? I want to kick him!

00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:05.000
C’mon, Ben. Take a three-pointer

00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:05.875
What are you afraid of?

00:34:05.875 --> 00:34:07.875
Oh, right...the fact that it definitely won’t go in

00:34:08.166 --> 00:34:10.750
This guy talks more trash than a young Kobe

00:34:10.750 --> 00:34:13.208
And also takes more bad shots than the old one

00:34:13.208 --> 00:34:15.291
At least I take shots, Benny one-point

00:34:15.291 --> 00:34:16.125
All right, just roll

00:34:16.125 --> 00:34:17.708
Some of us actually have real games to play

00:34:17.708 --> 00:34:18.291
Rude

00:34:18.666 --> 00:34:20.583
All right, I’ll fake the pass and then drive the lane

00:34:22.125 --> 00:34:23.250
Ugh, four

00:34:23.375 --> 00:34:24.375
Oof, that’s a turnover

00:34:24.375 --> 00:34:27.375
Ooh, mistakes like that can cost you Squire of the Year

00:34:27.750 --> 00:34:29.625
But I guess you can always try again next year

00:34:29.750 --> 00:34:30.666
Whose turn is it?

00:34:30.875 --> 00:34:32.625
I think it’s...Fultz. You’re up

00:34:32.916 --> 00:34:34.541
No, thanks. I’m not ready

00:34:34.750 --> 00:34:35.666
What’s happening here?

00:34:35.958 --> 00:34:37.541
Wait, you got the new 1K?

00:34:37.541 --> 00:34:38.416
Yeah, just came out

00:34:38.416 --> 00:34:39.958
But, it’s the end of the season

00:34:39.958 --> 00:34:42.125
Well, they’ve got to hand-carve all the graphics, Lonzo

00:34:42.375 --> 00:34:43.041
How is it?

00:34:43.041 --> 00:34:44.166
It’s pretty realistic

00:34:44.291 --> 00:34:46.416
Except they made my hair look painted on

00:34:46.416 --> 00:34:48.083
That’s because it does look painted on

00:34:48.083 --> 00:34:49.583
Oh, says Mona Lisa over here

00:34:49.583 --> 00:34:50.875
Well–can I see mine?

00:34:51.041 --> 00:34:52.625
Sure, let me find it

00:34:53.250 --> 00:34:54.250
Here’s Gordon Hayward

00:34:55.416 --> 00:34:56.250
Derrick Rose

00:34:56.250 --> 00:34:57.416
Ah, crap

00:34:58.416 --> 00:34:59.250
Klay Thompson

00:34:59.250 --> 00:35:01.375
Wow, graphics are uncanny

00:35:01.541 --> 00:35:02.958
Ah, here ya go, found Lonzo

00:35:03.041 --> 00:35:04.041
Oh thanks

00:35:04.041 --> 00:35:06.083
I think–wait, I think that’s Michael Carter-Williams

00:35:06.083 --> 00:35:06.458
Ugh

00:35:06.458 --> 00:35:07.041
[laughing]

00:35:07.041 --> 00:35:07.708
Very funny

00:35:08.041 --> 00:35:10.166
Lonzo, your rating’s actually pretty solid

00:35:10.291 --> 00:35:11.333
What about mine?

00:35:11.333 --> 00:35:12.333
Um

00:35:12.708 --> 00:35:13.541
You know

00:35:13.541 --> 00:35:15.250
This doesn’t look anything like me

00:35:15.250 --> 00:35:17.291
I guess they got lazy towards the back of the draft

00:35:17.291 --> 00:35:18.625
Well, what’s my rating?

00:35:18.625 --> 00:35:19.625
It's a 72

00:35:19.625 --> 00:35:22.583
What? I’m a 72 and Lonzo is an 80?

00:35:22.833 --> 00:35:24.458
Weren’t you in a bloody egg last year?

00:35:24.625 --> 00:35:26.916
Yeah, but that was like a special magical thing

00:35:26.916 --> 00:35:29.583
It’s probably changed, it’s just that we haven’t gotten the update raven

00:35:29.583 --> 00:35:30.916
Why don’t you just create your own knight?

00:35:30.916 --> 00:35:32.625
[sigh] I suppose I should

00:35:32.791 --> 00:35:34.250
Ugh, what are those?

00:35:34.250 --> 00:35:35.833
Those are your default 1K boots

00:35:35.833 --> 00:35:36.583
You start with them

00:35:36.583 --> 00:35:38.833
Nay, little me can’t be seen in these

00:35:38.833 --> 00:35:39.541
C’mon now

00:35:39.541 --> 00:35:42.458
You can purchase swag for your character from Ronnie 1k over there

00:35:42.791 --> 00:35:44.166
But I’ll warn you, it gets expensive

00:35:44.166 --> 00:35:45.916
500 coppers for boots?

00:35:46.375 --> 00:35:47.208
That’s madness

00:35:48.583 --> 00:35:50.458
Huh, well, you can’t put a price on style

00:35:50.875 --> 00:35:52.000
I’m going to fancy up me character

00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:53.000
Don’t start without me, alright?

00:35:55.208 --> 00:35:57.458
Hey, uh...you Ronnie 1K?

00:35:57.625 --> 00:35:58.375
That’s right, fam

00:35:58.583 --> 00:35:59.000
I am

00:35:59.208 --> 00:36:01.458
Well, I’d like to try out some of your haircuts please

00:36:01.458 --> 00:36:02.375
No samples!

00:36:02.375 --> 00:36:03.375
You try, you buy

00:36:03.375 --> 00:36:04.666
[scoffs] C'mon

00:36:04.958 --> 00:36:07.916
Well then, I’d like your finest fur coat for my little knight

00:36:08.125 --> 00:36:09.625
That’ll be 100 VC

00:36:10.208 --> 00:36:11.333
What–what's VC?

00:36:11.625 --> 00:36:12.750
Virtual coppers

00:36:12.916 --> 00:36:13.750
Uh, OK

00:36:13.958 --> 00:36:14.583
Here

00:36:14.583 --> 00:36:16.583
No, the–these are real coppers

00:36:16.708 --> 00:36:18.708
We only take virtual coppers

00:36:18.708 --> 00:36:20.833
Well then, how do I get virtual coppers?

00:36:20.833 --> 00:36:22.250
You pay me real coppers

00:36:22.250 --> 00:36:23.166
Are you–uh

00:36:23.416 --> 00:36:23.958
Right

00:36:24.416 --> 00:36:27.375
So, can I get 100 virtual coppers?

00:36:28.708 --> 00:36:29.708
There you are

00:36:30.875 --> 00:36:31.583
It’s empty

00:36:31.958 --> 00:36:34.708
Well, that’s cause you just went and spilled ‘em all over the floor

00:36:35.541 --> 00:36:36.750
Inbound to Lonzo

00:36:36.750 --> 00:36:37.916
What do I do?

00:36:37.916 --> 00:36:39.250
First, call out your move

00:36:39.250 --> 00:36:41.166
You’re on a team with Kuz and Donovan

00:36:41.416 --> 00:36:42.833
Markelle, you ready?

00:36:43.375 --> 00:36:44.166
No

00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:47.958
OK, I’ll send a full-court pass to Mitchell

00:36:47.958 --> 00:36:48.958
Alright, roll for it

00:36:50.500 --> 00:36:51.500
[dice on floor]

00:36:54.208 --> 00:36:55.083
OK

00:36:55.125 --> 00:36:59.416
Now, I’ve now picked up all 100 of my virtual coppers

00:36:59.416 --> 00:37:00.875
off the floor

00:37:00.875 --> 00:37:02.708
and I am handing them to you

00:37:03.250 --> 00:37:05.166
Please give me the fur coat

00:37:05.166 --> 00:37:06.041
[laughs]

00:37:06.041 --> 00:37:07.083
Nice try

00:37:07.083 --> 00:37:07.750
What?

00:37:07.750 --> 00:37:08.958
You're three short!

00:37:10.375 --> 00:37:13.083
So after the battle, you run into Matt Barnes

00:37:13.083 --> 00:37:17.875
He asks you if you’d like to join him on a 95-mile quest to kick Derek Fisher’s ass

00:37:17.875 --> 00:37:22.625
Do you say (A) Violence is never the answer or (B) But sometimes it is?

00:37:22.625 --> 00:37:24.791
Ugh, seven hells, this is so boring

00:37:24.791 --> 00:37:25.791
Can we skip this?

00:37:25.791 --> 00:37:26.791
Nope, sorry

00:37:26.791 --> 00:37:29.000
According to the rules, you can’t skip the woodcut scenes

00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:29.708
All right

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:33.708
Pure sharp, Demigod, Alpha Dog with Limitless Range

00:37:33.708 --> 00:37:35.041
Y’all are barbeque chicken

00:37:35.041 --> 00:37:36.166
Damn, Kuz

00:37:36.166 --> 00:37:38.916
And it only costs me 20,000 coppers and three of me goats

00:37:38.958 --> 00:37:40.583
All right Kuz, get in

00:37:40.958 --> 00:37:42.541
Fultz, the game is almost over

00:37:42.541 --> 00:37:43.750
You sure you don’t want to sub in?

00:37:43.750 --> 00:37:45.041
OK, I’m ready

00:37:45.291 --> 00:37:47.458
Um...hesi pull-up jimbo top of the key

00:37:48.916 --> 00:37:49.666
Oops

00:37:51.041 --> 00:37:51.333
All right

00:37:52.041 --> 00:37:53.041
My ball

00:37:53.583 --> 00:37:55.041
Two points away from the win

00:37:55.791 --> 00:37:57.750
I want to dunk over Ben Simmons

00:37:57.750 --> 00:38:01.500
[laughs] Uh, you know I’m a wee bit taller than Kevin Hart, right?

00:38:01.666 --> 00:38:03.208
All right, well, we’ll find out. Roll for it

00:38:05.125 --> 00:38:05.583
Boom!

00:38:05.916 --> 00:38:06.916
Eighteen!

00:38:06.916 --> 00:38:07.750
I win!

00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:09.791
Who says I’m not Squire of the Year?

00:38:10.041 --> 00:38:11.041
Actually, no

00:38:11.541 --> 00:38:12.291
You miss

00:38:12.291 --> 00:38:14.625
What do–miss? How? On an 18?

00:38:14.708 --> 00:38:16.458
Yeah, I mean your dunk rating

00:38:16.458 --> 00:38:18.416
It says here your dunk rating’s only 50

00:38:18.416 --> 00:38:18.750
A 50?!

00:38:18.750 --> 00:38:20.875
A 50?!
You need to roll a 20 to pull off a stunt like that

00:38:20.875 --> 00:38:22.291
Well that’s horse manure

00:38:22.291 --> 00:38:24.250
I won the bloody dunk contest!

00:38:24.250 --> 00:38:25.708
At least, I still haven’t received an update

00:38:25.708 --> 00:38:26.791
Hey, Ronnie!

00:38:26.791 --> 00:38:29.083
Fix your bloody 1K server ravens!

00:38:29.083 --> 00:38:31.250
I’ll bet by the time that update gets here

00:38:31.250 --> 00:38:33.000
I’ll have already have won Squire of the Year

00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:36.666
May I just mention that I’m the third-leading scorer on the second-best house in the East

00:38:36.666 --> 00:38:39.000
despite devastating injuries to our finest knights?

00:38:39.041 --> 00:38:40.750
I think that deserves some consideration

00:38:40.750 --> 00:38:42.375
Well, if either of your houses were in the West

00:38:42.375 --> 00:38:44.541
You wouldn’t even be considered for Squire of the Year

00:38:44.541 --> 00:38:46.708
Stop your squabbling, children

00:38:47.375 --> 00:38:50.166
The damn Squire of the Year award is overrated

00:38:50.791 --> 00:38:55.083
By this time next year, nobody will even remember who won

00:38:55.083 --> 00:38:56.875
Oh, yeah? And who the hell are you?

00:39:09.458 --> 00:39:12.083
But, why must you leave?

00:39:12.083 --> 00:39:14.083
I’m a free agent now

00:39:14.083 --> 00:39:15.541
Will you be back?

00:39:15.666 --> 00:39:17.875
Aye. One way or another

00:39:18.083 --> 00:39:20.125
But...but, where will you go?

00:39:20.500 --> 00:39:22.583
I will raise the sails of me heart

00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:24.375
and let the winds of destiny blow where they–

00:39:24.375 --> 00:39:25.166
and let the winds of destiny blow where they–
-C'mon mate

00:39:25.166 --> 00:39:26.666
You’re wearing a Lakers tunic

00:39:26.666 --> 00:39:27.958
Well...yeah

00:39:28.125 --> 00:39:31.416
Paul, you realize House Lakers are bad, right?

00:39:31.416 --> 00:39:34.000
Russ, in my years, I’ve come to accept 

00:39:34.000 --> 00:39:37.291
that I will lose in the playoffs no matter where I go

00:39:37.291 --> 00:39:39.458
But Los Angeles has a beach

00:39:39.458 --> 00:39:40.458
[sniffles]

00:39:40.458 --> 00:39:41.458
[sniffles]
Alright, well

00:39:41.875 --> 00:39:45.208
I must be going. Grunion season is upon us

00:39:45.916 --> 00:39:46.750
Yah yah!

00:39:48.541 --> 00:39:49.875
Surf's up, mate

00:39:52.750 --> 00:39:57.708
Aw, c’mon now, Russ. Don’t worry. I’m not gonna go anywhere.

00:39:57.708 --> 00:39:58.708
[sob]

00:40:04.375 --> 00:40:06.833
[murmur]
I actually kind of liked Pusha T’s diss track

00:40:06.833 --> 00:40:08.250
[murmur]
I don’t wanna tell Drake, though

00:40:08.250 --> 00:40:11.041
[murmur]
I thought he went too far talking about Drake’s parents and all

00:40:11.083 --> 00:40:11.875
[bang]

00:40:11.875 --> 00:40:13.000
Shh, shh, Drake wants to say something

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:15.333
Shh, shh, Drake wants to say something
[bang]

00:40:16.791 --> 00:40:19.583
You’re wondering why I brought you all here

00:40:20.291 --> 00:40:24.208
After all, we just had a feast to celebrate our No. 1 seed

00:40:24.208 --> 00:40:28.833
And since when does Old Drake give two feasts in a single fortnight?

00:40:29.083 --> 00:40:30.666
[murmur]
Yeah, we love you Drake!

00:40:31.458 --> 00:40:33.875
Well it’s no good being Lord of the Six

00:40:33.875 --> 00:40:37.750
if you can’t celebrate a 
first-round victory with your woes

00:40:37.750 --> 00:40:40.333
The great knights of House Raptors!

00:40:40.333 --> 00:40:41.791
Yeah!

00:40:41.791 --> 00:40:42.833
Yeah!
Yeah, we're the North!

00:40:42.833 --> 00:40:46.708
Sure, the scribes, they don’t want to talk about us

00:40:46.791 --> 00:40:48.666
[grunts]

00:40:48.708 --> 00:40:50.833
Some dingy house in the North

00:40:50.833 --> 00:40:52.083
[laughs]

00:40:52.083 --> 00:40:57.291
They all just want to talk about The Process

00:40:57.291 --> 00:40:57.833
Boo!

00:40:57.833 --> 00:40:58.791
Boo!
Ben Simmons can suck my–

00:40:58.791 --> 00:41:01.875
And the washed up King LeBron

00:41:01.875 --> 00:41:03.541
Boo!
I hate LeBron!

00:41:03.541 --> 00:41:11.041
Well I say, LeBron can have his stupid Feast of the East

00:41:11.041 --> 00:41:12.458
Yeah!

00:41:12.458 --> 00:41:16.750
This year, the North will feast

00:41:16.791 --> 00:41:18.416
on the East!

00:41:18.416 --> 00:41:21.458
[cheer]

00:41:21.458 --> 00:41:24.291
But first, a toast!

00:41:25.416 --> 00:41:27.833
No more of that southern horse piss

00:41:27.833 --> 00:41:28.500
No more of that southern horse piss

00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:31.458
Proper wine for proper knights

00:41:31.916 --> 00:41:35.250
Courtesy of your Champagne Papi

00:41:36.208 --> 00:41:37.458
Stand together!

00:41:38.750 --> 00:41:41.291
North...over everything!

00:41:41.666 --> 00:41:43.750
North over everything!

00:41:50.041 --> 00:41:51.166
Not you

00:41:51.541 --> 00:41:54.291
I’m not wasting good wine on a damn horse

00:41:55.708 --> 00:42:02.125
Here, to the men who slaughtered
the Wizards in only six games

00:42:02.125 --> 00:42:03.458
That's right, we did!
Yeah, they suck!

00:42:04.916 --> 00:42:07.916
Yes, yes. Cheer.

00:42:07.916 --> 00:42:10.208
Brave men. All of you

00:42:10.458 --> 00:42:13.208
Took six games to beat a house

00:42:13.208 --> 00:42:17.458
that had three less wins this year than the Nuggets

00:42:17.791 --> 00:42:19.500
That's right! Oh...

00:42:20.958 --> 00:42:24.833
Haven’t you little northern knights learned?

00:42:24.833 --> 00:42:28.291
After all these years, 

00:42:28.291 --> 00:42:31.125
killing pawns means nothing

00:42:31.166 --> 00:42:35.000
if you can’t fell the King

00:42:35.000 --> 00:42:37.541
[choking]

00:42:37.541 --> 00:42:39.083
Am I dying?

00:42:39.083 --> 00:42:42.541
No, we're just choking. You'll get used to it.

00:42:49.250 --> 00:42:54.000
When people ask you what happened here, tell them King James still rules the East

00:42:55.416 --> 00:42:58.708
Also, tell them I’m better than Michael Jordan

00:43:18.916 --> 00:43:21.833
King James has slaughtered the Raptors in four battles

00:43:22.708 --> 00:43:25.916
But I thought The Messiah Ujiri could walk on water

00:43:25.916 --> 00:43:28.500
Wah! Any other Master of Trades would be torched

00:43:28.958 --> 00:43:32.041
The King then conquered Bostonia after a grueling seven battles

00:43:32.291 --> 00:43:34.833
Wah! Tatum’s ceiling is still lower than Fultz

00:43:35.083 --> 00:43:36.000
Hm, what’s this?

00:43:36.500 --> 00:43:39.333
Bryan Colangelo is dumb and his collars are too big, ugh

00:43:39.333 --> 00:43:42.666
Wah! Brian’s collars are normal-sized, find a new slant

00:43:42.666 --> 00:43:43.750
Aw, thank you Honest Abe

00:43:43.750 --> 00:43:46.875
Wah! Bryan is a class act! I worked with him. So classy!

00:43:46.875 --> 00:43:51.541
You know, when my wife decided to raise little burner ravens, I had my doubts

00:43:51.541 --> 00:43:53.833
But I’ve really grown to love you all

00:43:53.833 --> 00:43:55.208
Even you, little Jacob Reuben

00:43:55.208 --> 00:43:58.833
Wah! Bryan you’re so attractive. Jahlil failed his physical, did you know that?

00:43:58.833 --> 00:44:02.333
Oh, Phila1234567, did someone mention me?

00:44:03.208 --> 00:44:05.375
Hmm...from Joel

00:44:05.375 --> 00:44:09.416
Lord Hinkie is better and smarter than you, Eric Jr.

00:44:09.416 --> 00:44:10.666
Eric Jr.?!

00:44:10.666 --> 00:44:12.291
Wah! Wish I had a medium-sized ladder!

00:44:12.291 --> 00:44:13.041
Shh, shh!

00:44:13.041 --> 00:44:16.791
What’s this? The Curious Case of Bryan Long Collars?

00:44:17.208 --> 00:44:18.250
Wah! Normal Collar!

00:44:18.250 --> 00:44:19.166
Shut up, shut up!

00:44:20.125 --> 00:44:21.083
It's long

00:44:21.125 --> 00:44:22.500
Bryan, are you in there?

00:44:22.500 --> 00:44:23.416
I’m busy!

00:44:23.416 --> 00:44:28.458
Maester Detrick of the Ringer Guild has published a paper 
accusing you of using burner ravens

00:44:28.458 --> 00:44:29.458
Is this true?

00:44:29.458 --> 00:44:31.250
What? No, that’s ridiculous

00:44:31.250 --> 00:44:32.583
Sorry, Honest Abe

00:44:32.583 --> 00:44:33.916
Wah! Class Act!

00:44:33.916 --> 00:44:34.916
Where is he getting all this?

00:44:34.916 --> 00:44:38.291
Some analytics wizard did an analysis of the scrolls

00:44:38.291 --> 00:44:39.708
Analytics wizard?

00:44:40.125 --> 00:44:41.208
No...

00:44:41.208 --> 00:44:41.666
[gasps]

00:44:41.666 --> 00:44:45.416
Hinkie!

00:44:57.333 --> 00:44:58.583
[knock, knock]

00:45:01.458 --> 00:45:03.333
That you, Lord Ainge?

00:45:04.625 --> 00:45:07.041
[muffled] Teamwork

00:45:08.458 --> 00:45:11.666
Gordon? Another late night of boardgaming?

00:45:15.458 --> 00:45:21.000
Alright, Terry. I think maybe you’re taking this “scary” thing a bit too far, no?

00:45:24.250 --> 00:45:26.291
Your Grace? What are you doing here?

00:45:26.541 --> 00:45:27.000
Dah!

00:45:27.000 --> 00:45:27.541
Aah!

00:45:27.541 --> 00:45:29.000
[pant] Hwah!

00:45:32.958 --> 00:45:35.125
It is your time

00:45:37.875 --> 00:45:41.000
Spurs of the East

00:45:41.833 --> 00:45:46.458
[screams in pain]

